Package: rayplot
Type: Package
Title: Toy Interactive Plotting with raylib
Version: 0.0.1
Authors@R: person("Konrad", "Krämer", email = "konrad_kraemer@yahoo.de", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A toy package that opens a raylib window from R and draws an
    interactive scatter plot with mouse pan and scroll zoom. The render loop
    is driven cooperatively from R's event loop via 'later', so the R console
    stays usable while the window is open. Not production ready; a playground
    for wiring raylib into R.
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
Imports: later, ggplot2, grDevices, stats, jsonlite, utils
Suggests: shiny, htmltools
SystemRequirements: A C toolchain and OpenGL + X11 development headers
        on Linux (e.g. libgl1-mesa-dev, xorg-dev). raylib itself is
        vendored in src/raylib (raylib 5.5, zlib licence) and built
        with the package; no system raylib install is needed.
NeedsCompilation: yes
Packaged: 2026-09-09 10:20:53 UTC; konrad
Author: Konrad Krämer [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Konrad Krämer <konrad_kraemer@yahoo.de>
